        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n     4→    \"title\": \"Devin Review API & MCP Enhancements\",\n     5→    \"description\": \"Devin released numerous updates throughout early 2026 including the Devin Review API for programmatic PR reviews, Mermaid diagram rendering, per-PR auto-review toggles, sidebar session notifications, service user permission management, MCP secret scoping, and Ask Devin in PR discussions. Major features include stacked review permissions, skill slash commands, auto-fix with CI checks integration, and session categorization.\",\n     6→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\",\n     8→    \"date\": \"2026-05-15\",\n     9→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    10→  },\n    11→  {\n    12→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    13→    \"title\": \"Cloud Agent Development Environments\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"Cursor released major updates on May 13, 2026, introducing development environments for cloud agents with multi-repo support, Dockerfile-based configuration with build secrets, and improved agent-led environment setup. Also released Microsoft Teams integration and Bugbot effort level customization on May 11, followed by PR review experience improvements and parallel plan execution on May 7.\",\n    15→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    16→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    17→    \"date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    18→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    19→      {\n    20→        \"quote\": \"Claude Code vs Cursor: two philosophies, not two versions of the same thing - Claude Code is a terminal-native execution agent, Cursor is an AI-augmented IDE\",\n    21→        \"source\": \"Emergent.sh / Reddit\",\n    22→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n    23→      },\n    24→      {\n    25→        \"quote\": \"Cursor acts as a partner where you stay in control, while Claude Code runs 30-minute autonomous sessions\",\n    26→        \"source\": \"Medium\",\n    27→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n    28→      }\n    29→    ]\n    30→  },\n    31→  {\n    32→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n    33→    \"title\": \"v0.42.0: Enhanced Memory & Real-Time Voice\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Gemini CLI v0.42.0 (May 12, 2026) introduces Auto Memory Inbox to automatically capture context from executed commands and files, improved voice input with recording visualizer and output streaming, history command with timeline view and session filtering, and performance optimizations.\",\n    35→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    36→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/changelog\",\n    37→    \"date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    38→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    39→  },\n    40→  {\n    41→    \"productName\": \"Continue\",\n    42→    \"title\": \"v1.3.38: Config Management and Security Fixes\",\n    43→    \"description\": \"Continue released v1.3.38-vscode with features including .continue/configs support, session history filtering by workspace directory, and critical security vulnerability resolutions. Recent versions added ClawRouter provider for cost-optimized model routing, Responses API opt-out option, OpenRouter improvements with Gemini 3 tool support, and extensive bug fixes for JetBrains and VSCode integrations.\",\n    44→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    45→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\",\n    46→    \"date\": \"2026-05-10\",\n    47→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    48→  },\n    49→  {\n    50→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n    51→    \"title\": \"May 2026: Chrome Extension & Remote Control\",\n    52→    \"description\": \"Codex CLI released May 2026 updates including Chrome extension for browser automation, remote control capabilities for connecting to remote sessions, CLI 0.130.0 with enhanced stability and new integrations. Focus on cross-platform compatibility and improved user experience for web development workflows.\",\n    53→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    54→    \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/codex-cli/changelog\",\n    55→    \"date\": \"2026-05-09\",\n    56→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    57→  },\n    58→  {\n    59→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    60→    \"title\": \"Week 19 Updates: Plugin Support & Enhanced Git Workflows\",\n    61→    \"description\": \"Claude Code v2.1.128–v2.1.136 (May 4–8, 2026) introduces plugin loading from .zip archives and URLs, worktree baseRef configuration, auto mode hard deny rules, and hooks that see active effort level. Previous weeks brought Windows PowerShell support, ultrareview cloud code review, and project purge tools.\",\n    62→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    63→    \"url\": \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\",\n    64→    \"date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    65→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    66→      {\n    67→        \"quote\": \"Cursor is great when you want agent-level edits but also need to eyeball a bunch of files side by side\",\n    68→        \"source\": \"Reddit r/AI_Agents\",\n    69→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n    70→      }\n    71→    ]\n    72→  },\n    73→  {\n    74→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n    75→    \"title\": \"April 2026: Agentic Workflows in VS Code\",\n    76→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot released April 2026 updates for Visual Studio Code (v1.116-v1.119, released May 6) focusing on agentic workflows with cloud agent sessions, custom agent capabilities, and Visual Studio April updates. GPT-4.1 was deprecated across Copilot experiences with GPT-5.5 as the recommended alternative.\",\n    77→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    78→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-05-06-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-code-april-releases/\",\n    79→    \"date\": \"2026-05-06\",\n    80→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n    84→    \"title\": \"v0.41.0: Code Index & Compact Output\",\n    85→    \"description\": \"Gemini CLI v0.41.0 (May 5, 2026) added automatic code indexing on startup with configurable depth control, context menu improvements with global shortcuts and favorite prompts, compact output mode for improved readability, and ability to restart conversations from history.\",\n    86→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/changelog\",\n    88→    \"date\": \"2026-05-05\",\n    89→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    90→  },\n    91→  {\n    92→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n    93→    \"title\": \"AI-Agentic IDE with Cascade Integration\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Windsurf is an AI-agentic IDE featuring Cascade for deep codebase context awareness, collaborative editing with real-time AI agent participation, predictive editing for multi-step refactoring, and natural language-to-code transformation. Integrates with popular editors and supports multiple LLM providers.\",\n    95→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    96→    \"url\": \"https://windsurf.ai/overview\",\n    97→    \"date\": \"2026-05-01\",\n    98→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    99→  }\n   100→]\n   101→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
