lass=\"item\">\n   313→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   314→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/open-computer-use\">Open Computer Use</a>\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   317→                        Open-source framework for computer-use AI agents that enables autonomous interaction with desktop interfaces and applications.\n   318→                    </div>\n   319→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   320→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI agent framework</span>\n   321→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   322→                    </div>\n   323→                </div>\n   324→\n   325→                <div class=\"item\">\n   326→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   327→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/open-browser-use\">Open Browser Use</a>\n   328→                    </div>\n   329→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   330→                        Open-source browser automation agent framework for building AI agents that can navigate and interact with web pages autonomously.\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   333→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI agent framework</span>\n   334→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                </div>\n   337→\n   338→                <div class=\"item\">\n   339→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   340→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/openclaw-os\">Openclaw OS</a>\n   341→                    </div>\n   342→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   343→                        Development platform that turns one-off AI chat interactions into persistent, reusable applications. Bridges the gap between conversational AI and deployable software.\n   344→                    </div>\n   345→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   346→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI development platform</span>\n   347→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   348→                    </div>\n   349→                </div>\n   350→\n   351→                <div class=\"item\">\n   352→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   353→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/claudy\">Claudy</a>\n   354→                    </div>\n   355→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   356→                        Multi-session, multi-account management interface for Claude Code. Provides a proper workspace environment with enhanced session handling.\n   357→                    </div>\n   358→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   359→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI code agent</span>\n   360→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   361→                    </div>\n   362→                </div>\n   363→\n   364→                <div class=\"item\">\n   365→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   366→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/latitude-for-claude-code\">Latitude for Claude Code</a>\n   367→                    </div>\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   369→                        Observability and token usage tracking tool for Claude Code. Shows where Claude Code burns tokens to help optimize costs.\n   370→                    </div>\n   371→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   372→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding observability</span>\n   373→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   374→                    </div>\n   375→                </div>\n   376→\n   377→                <div class=\"item\">\n   378→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   379→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/warp\">Warp</a>\n   380→                    </div>\n   381→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   382→                        Open-source agentic development environment built with community collaboration. Represents a new approach to IDEs with AI-first architecture.\n   383→                    </div>\n   384→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   385→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   386→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                </div>\n   389→\n   390→                <div class=\"item\">\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   392→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/graphbit-prflow\">Graphbit PRFlow</a>\n   393→                    </div>\n   394→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   395→                        AI-powered code reviewer for pull requests that catches issues that traditional reviewers miss. Integrates into GitHub workflows.\n   396→                    </div>\n   397→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   398→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI code review</span>\n   399→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   400→                    </div>\n   401→                </div>\n   402→\n   403→                <div class=\"item\">\n   404→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   405→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/weavable\">Weavable</a>\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   408→                        Persistent work context infrastructure that gives every AI agent access to shared project memory and context.\n   409→                    </div>\n   410→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   411→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI memory infrastructure</span>\n   412→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                </div>\n   415→\n   416→                <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   418→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/display-dev\">display.dev</a>\n   419→                    </div>\n   420→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   421→                        Deployment platform that publishes AI agent-generated HTML behind company authentication. Enables secure sharing of agent-created web content.\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   424→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI deployment</span>\n   425→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   426→                    </div>\n   427→                </div>\n   428→            </section>\n   429→\n   430→            <section class=\"column\">\n   431→                <div class=\"column-header\">Whitelist Updates (6)</div>\n   432→\n   433→                <div class=\"item\">\n   434→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   435→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span>\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   438→                        <strong>Week 19 Updates: Plugin Support & Enhanced Git Workflows</strong><br>\n   439→                        v2.1.128–v2.1.136 (May 4–8) introduces plugin loading from .zip archives and URLs, worktree baseRef configuration, auto mode hard deny rules, and hooks that see active effort level. Previous weeks brought Windows PowerShell support, ultrareview cloud code review, and project purge tools.\n   440→                    </div>\n   441→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   442→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-05-08</span> | <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\">Release Notes</a>\n   443→                    </div>\n   444→                </div>\n   445→\n   446→                <div class=\"item\">\n   447→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   448→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   451→                        <strong>Cloud Agent Development Environments</strong><br>\n   452→                        May 13 updates introducing development environments for cloud agents with multi-repo support, Dockerfile-based configuration with build secrets, and improved agent-led environment setup. Also released Microsoft Teams integration and Bugbot effort level customization on May 11, followed by PR review experience improvements and parallel plan execution on May 7.\n   453→                    </div>\n   454→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   455→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-05-13</span> | <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Changelog</a>\n   456→                    </div>\n   457→                    <div class=\"quote\">\n   458→                        \"Claude Code vs Cursor: two philosophies, not two versions of the same thing - Claude Code is a terminal-native execution agent, Cursor is an AI-augmented IDE\"\n   459→                    </div>\n   460→                </div>\n   461→\n   462→                <div class=\"item\">\n   463→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   464→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Continue</span>\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   467→                        <strong>v1.3.38: Config Management and Security Fixes</strong><br>\n   468→                        Released v1.3.38-vscode with .continue/configs support, session history filtering by workspace directory, and critical security vulnerability resolutions. Recent versions added ClawRouter provider for cost-optimized model routing, Responses API opt-out option, OpenRouter improvements with Gemini 3 tool support.\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   471→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-05-10</span> | <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\">GitHub</a>\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                </div>\n   474→\n   475→                <div class=\"item\">\n   476→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   477→                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   480→                        <strong>April 2026: Agentic Workflows in VS Code</strong><br>\n   481→                        v1.116-v1.119 (released May 6) focusing on agentic workflows with cloud agent sessions, custom agent capabilities, and Visual Studio April updates. GPT-4.1 was deprecated across Copilot experiences with GPT-5.5 as the recommended alternative.\n   482→                    </div>\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   484→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-05-06</span> | <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-05-06-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-code-april-releases/\">Blog</a>\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                </div>\n   487→\n   488→                <div class=\"item\">\n   489→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   490→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Devin</span>\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   493→                        <strong>Devin Review API & MCP Enhancements</strong><br>\n   494→                        Updates throughout early 2026 including Devin Review API for programmatic PR reviews, Mermaid diagram rendering, per-PR auto-review toggles, sidebar session notifications, service user permission management, MCP secret scoping, and Ask Devin in PR discussions.\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   497→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-05-15</span> | <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\">Release Notes</a>\n   498→                    </div>\n   499→                </div>\n   500→\n   501→                <div class=\"item\">\n   502→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   503→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span>\n   504→                    </div>\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   506→                        <strong>v0.86.0: GPT-5 and Grok-4 Support</strong><br>\n   507→                        Added support for all GPT-5 models, Grok-4 via xAI and OpenRouter, Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite Preview, and improved commit message output readability. Recent versions (v0.83.0-v0.85.0) added extensive new model support including Gemini 2.5 Pro/Flash series, o1-pro, o3-pro, Deepseek models, thinking tokens support, and 130 new programming languages.\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   510→                        <span class=\"source\">2026-04-14</span> | <a href=\"https://github.com/aider-ai/aider/releases\">GitHub</a>\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                </div>\n   513→            </section>\n   514→\n   515→            <section class=\"column\">\n   516→                <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights (17)</div>\n   517→\n   518→                <div class=\"item\">\n   519→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   520→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</span>\n   521→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40823421\">The US is winning the AI race in commercialization</a></span>\n   522→                    </div>\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   524→                        Analysis arguing that the US is winning the AI race where it matters most: commercialization and practical application of AI technologies.\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   527→                        <span class=\"source\">Hacker News</span> | 2026-05-14\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                </div>\n   530→\n   531→                <div class=\"item\">\n   532→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   533→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">News</span>\n   534→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/notion-ai-agent-platform/\">Notion turns workspace into AI agent hub</a></span>\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   537→                        Notion launched a developer platform that transforms its workspace into a hub for AI agents, allowing developers to build and integrate AI agents directly.\n   538→                    </div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   540→                        <span class=\"source\">Sarah Perez</span> | 2026-05-13\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→                </div>\n   543→\n   544→                <div class=\"item\">\n   545→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   546→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">News</span>\n   547→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/vapi-voice-ai-valuation/\">AI voice startup Vapi hits $500M valuation</a></span>\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   550→                        AI voice startup Vapi reached a $500M valuation after winning Amazon Ring as a customer over 40 competitors.\n   551→                    </div>\n   552→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   553→                        <span class=\"source\">Jagmeet Singh</span> | 2026-05-13\n   554→                    </div>\n   555→                </div>\n   556→\n   557→                <div class=\"item\">\n   558→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   559→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">News</span>\n   560→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/adaption-autoscientist-ai/\">Adaption aims big with AutoScientist</a></span>\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   563→                        Adaption announced AutoScientist, an AI tool designed to help models train themselves, representing advances in self-improving AI systems.\n   564→                    </div>\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   566→                        <span class=\"source\">Russell Brandom</span> | 2026-05-13\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                </div>\n   569→\n   570→                <div class=\"item\">\n   571→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   572→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Interview</span>\n   573→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/anthropic-cat-wu-interview/\">Anthropic Cat Wu on AI anticipating user needs</a></span>\n   574→                    </div>\n   575→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   576→                        Anthropic's Cat Wu discussed the future of AI systems that can anticipate user needs before users themselves know what they are.\n   577→                    </div>\n   578→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   579→                        <span class=\"source\">Lucas Ropek</span> | 2026-05-13\n   580→                    </div>\n   581→                </div>\n   582→\n   583→                <div class=\"item\">\n   584→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   585→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</span>\n   586→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812345\">Leaving GitHub for Forgejo</a></span>\n   587→                    </div>\n   588→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   589→                        Developer discusses reasons for leaving GitHub for Forgejo, a self-hosted Git forge. Raises questions about platform lock-in and open source alternatives.\n   590→                    </div>\n   591→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   592→                        <span class=\"source\">Hacker News</span> | 2026-05-13\n   593→                    </div>\n   594→                </div>\n   595→\n   596→                <div class=\"item\">\n   597→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   598→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">News</span>\n   599→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/gm-layoffs-it-ai-skills/\">GM lays off IT workers to hire AI specialists</a></span>\n   600→                    </div>\n   601→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   602→                        General Motors laid off hundreds of IT workers to hire employees with stronger AI skills, reflecting a broader trend of workforce restructuring.\n   603→                    </div>\n   604→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   605→                        <span class=\"source\">Kirsten Korosec</span> | 2026-05-12\n   606→                    </div>\n   607→                </div>\n   608→\n   609→                <div class=\"item\">\n   610→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   611→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">News</span>\n   612→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/google-android-agentic-ai-widgets/\">Google brings agentic AI to Android</a></span>\n   613→                    </div>\n   614→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   615→                        Google announced agentic AI capabilities and 'vibe-coded' widgets for Android, allowing users to create widgets through natural language prompts.\n   616→                    </div>\n   617→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   618→                        <span class=\"source\">Ivan Mehta</span> | 2026-05-12\n   619→                    </div>\n   620→                </div>\n   621→\n   622→                <div class=\"item\">\n   623→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   624→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">News</span>\n   625→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/digg-ai-news-aggregator/\">Digg relaunches as AI news aggregator</a></span>\n   626→                    </div>\n   627→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   628→                        Social news pioneer Digg relaunched as an AI-powered news aggregator, attempting to reinvent itself for the AI era.\n   629→                    </div>\n   630→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   631→                        <span class=\"source\">Sarah Perez</span> | 2026-05-12\n   632→                    </div>\n   633→                </div>\n   634→\n   635→                <div class=\"item\">\n   636→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   637→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Podcast</span>\n   638→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/608\">Amelia Wattenberger on Intent and agent-first design</a></span>\n   639→                    </div>\n   640→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   641→                        Discussion on the identity crisis developers face as agents take over, the redesign of developer tooling for agent-first workflows. Key insight: prototyping got easier but finishing got harder.\n   642→                    </div>\n   643→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   644→                        <span class=\"source\">The Changelog</span> | 2026-05-12\n   645→                    </div>\n   646→                </div>\n   647→\n   648→                <div class=\"item\">\n   649→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   650→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Podcast</span>\n   651→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/607\">Astral joins OpenAI</a></span>\n   652→                    </div>\n   653→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   654→                        Discussion about Astral joining OpenAI and what this signals about the center of gravity moving for developer tools. Also covered: LiteLLM supply-chain attack, OpenCode, and Rust's reality check.\n   655→                    </div>\n   656→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   657→                        <span class=\"source\">The Changelog</span> | 2026-05-10\n   658→                    </div>\n   659→                </div>\n   660→\n   661→                <div class=\"item\">\n   662→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   663→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</span>\n   664→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40789234\">A History of IDEs at Google</a></span>\n   665→                    </div>\n   666→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   667→                        Detailed discussion about the evolution of Integrated Development Environments used internally at Google.\n   668→                    </div>\n   669→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   670→                        <span class=\"source\">Hacker News</span> | 2026-05-10\n   671→                    </div>\n   672→                </div>\n   673→\n   674→                <div class=\"item\">\n   675→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   676→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Podcast</span>\n   677→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/606\">Tailscale's TSIDP, TSNet, and Aperture</a></span>\n   678→                    </div>\n   679→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   680→                        Interview with Tailscale co-founder David Carney about TSIDP (clickless auth), TSNet apps, and Aperture - Tailscale's private AI gateway for API key management and agent security.\n   681→                    </div>\n   682→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   683→                        <span class=\"source\">The Changelog</span> | 2026-05-09\n   684→                    </div>\n   685→                </div>\n   686→\n   687→                <div class=\"item\">\n   688→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   689→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Podcast</span>\n   690→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/605\">GPT-5.4, AWS attacks, and brain cells play DOOM</a></span>\n   691→                    </div>\n   692→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   693→                        Iran allegedly bombed AWS data centers to take down Claude, OpenAI released GPT-5.4 with significant coding improvements, and living brain cells were taught to play DOOM.\n   694→                    </div>\n   695→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   696→                        <span class=\"source\">The Changelog</span> | 2026-05-08\n   697→                    </div>\n   698→                </div>\n   699→\n   700→                <div class=\"item\">\n   701→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   702→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Podcast</span>\n   703→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/604\">Burke Holland on Opus 4.5 and AI coding</a></span>\n   704→                    </div>\n   705→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   706→                        Burke Holland from GitHub Copilot discusses how Opus 4.5 changed everything in AI coding, the 2x usage bump from Claude, and GPT-5.3 Codex living up to the hype.\n   707→                    </div>\n   708→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   709→                        <span class=\"source\">The Changelog</span> | 2026-05-08\n   710→                    </div>\n   711→                </div>\n   712→\n   713→                <div class=\"item\">\n   714→                    <div class=\"insight-header\">\n   715→                        <span class=\"insight-type\">Technical</span>\n   716→                        <span class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/8/html/\">The Unreasonable Effectiveness of HTML</a></span>\n   717→                    </div>\n   718→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   719→                        Thariq Shihipar (Claude Code team) advocates for HTML over Markdown as LLM output format. HTML enables SVG diagrams, interactive widgets, and richer explanations.\n   720→                    </div>\n   721→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   722→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span> | 2026-05-08\n   723→                    </div>\n   724→                </div>\n   725→            </section>\n   726→        </main>\n   727→\n   728→        <footer>\n   729→            <a href=\"#\">Back to top</a> |\n   730→            Generated by AgentDaily |\n   731→            <a href=\"https://github.com/agentdaily/agentdaily\">GitHub</a>\n   732→        </footer>\n   733→    </div>\n   734→</body>\n   735→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
