n   296→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/warp\" target=\"_blank\">Warp</a></div>\n   297→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source agentic development environment built with community collaboration. AI-first architecture with community-driven development.</div>\n   298→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   299→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   300→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   301→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   302→                    </div>\n   303→                </div>\n   304→\n   305→                <div class=\"item\">\n   306→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/robrain\" target=\"_blank\">RoBrain</a></div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source shared AI memory system that captures team decisions and rejected alternatives to prevent agents from repeating mistakes.</div>\n   308→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   309→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   310→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   311→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   312→                    </div>\n   313→                </div>\n   314→\n   315→                <div class=\"item\">\n   316→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/weavable\" target=\"_blank\">Weavable</a></div>\n   317→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Persistent work context infrastructure that gives every AI agent access to shared project memory and context for multi-agent workflows.</div>\n   318→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   319→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   320→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   321→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   322→                    </div>\n   323→                </div>\n   324→\n   325→                <div class=\"item\">\n   326→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/claudy\" target=\"_blank\">Claudy</a></div>\n   327→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Multi-session, multi-account management interface for Claude Code with enhanced session handling and account switching.</div>\n   328→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   329→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   330→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   331→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   332→                    </div>\n   333→                </div>\n   334→\n   335→                <div class=\"item\">\n   336→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/open-computer-use\" target=\"_blank\">Open Computer Use</a></div>\n   337→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source framework for computer-use AI agents that enables autonomous interaction with desktop interfaces and applications.</div>\n   338→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   339→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   340→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   341→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   342→                    </div>\n   343→                </div>\n   344→\n   345→                <div class=\"item\">\n   346→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/open-browser-use\" target=\"_blank\">Open Browser Use</a></div>\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source browser automation agent framework for building AI agents that navigate and interact with web pages autonomously.</div>\n   348→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   349→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   350→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   351→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                </div>\n   354→\n   355→                <div class=\"item\">\n   356→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/asteroid\" target=\"_blank\">Asteroid</a></div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Rapid AI agent builder that creates Browser, Linux, and Windows AI agents in seconds. Lowers barrier to cross-platform autonomous systems.</div>\n   358→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   359→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   360→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   361→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                </div>\n   364→\n   365→                <div class=\"item\">\n   366→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/raindrop-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">Raindrop Workshop</a></div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source, free, local debugger specifically designed for AI agents. Inspect and debug AI agent behavior locally without cloud dependencies.</div>\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   369→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI developer tools</span>\n   370→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   371→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                </div>\n   374→\n   375→                <div class=\"item\">\n   376→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/comie-dev\" target=\"_blank\">Comie.dev</a></div>\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Production context layer for AI coding agents connecting them to production infrastructure including logs, databases, and error tracking.</div>\n   378→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   379→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   380→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   381→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   382→                    </div>\n   383→                </div>\n   384→\n   385→                <div class=\"item\">\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/graphbit-prflow\" target=\"_blank\">Graphbit PRFlow</a></div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI-powered code reviewer for pull requests that catches issues traditional reviewers miss. Integrates into GitHub workflows.</div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   389→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   390→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   391→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   392→                    </div>\n   393→                </div>\n   394→\n   395→                <div class=\"item\">\n   396→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/latitude-for-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Latitude for Claude Code</a></div>\n   397→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Observability and token usage tracking tool for Claude Code. Shows where Claude Code burns tokens to optimize costs.</div>\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   399→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI developer tools</span>\n   400→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   401→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   402→                    </div>\n   403→                </div>\n   404→\n   405→                <div class=\"item\">\n   406→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com\" target=\"_blank\">Agent FM for Claude Code & Codex</a></div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"item-description\">File manager and agent interface for Claude Code and Codex that enhances file navigation and manipulation capabilities.</div>\n   408→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   409→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   410→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   411→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   412→                    </div>\n   413→                </div>\n   414→\n   415→                <div class=\"item\">\n   416→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/display-dev\" target=\"_blank\">display.dev</a></div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Deployment platform that publishes AI agent-generated HTML behind company authentication. Secure sharing with enterprise access controls.</div>\n   418→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   419→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   420→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   421→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                </div>\n   424→\n   425→                <div class=\"item\">\n   426→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/openclaw-os\" target=\"_blank\">Openclaw OS</a></div>\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Development platform that turns one-off AI chat interactions into persistent, reusable applications. Bridges conversational AI and deployable software.</div>\n   428→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   429→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI development platform</span>\n   430→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   431→                        <span class=\"badge badge-new\">NEW</span>\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                </div>\n   434→            </section>\n   435→\n   436→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   437→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   438→                <h2>Product Updates <span class=\"section-count\">(9)</span></h2>\n   439→\n   440→                <div class=\"item\">\n   441→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">Devin</a></div>\n   442→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Review API & MCP Enhancements. Devin released numerous updates including Devin Review API for programmatic PR reviews, Mermaid diagram rendering, per-PR auto-review toggles, sidebar session notifications, service user permission management, MCP secret scoping, and Ask Devin in PR discussions.</div>\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   444→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   445→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   446→                        2026-05-15\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                </div>\n   449→\n   450→                <div class=\"item\">\n   451→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a></div>\n   452→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Cloud Agent Development Environments. Major updates introducing development environments for cloud agents with multi-repo support, Dockerfile-based configuration with build secrets, and improved agent-led environment setup. Also released Microsoft Teams integration and Bugbot effort level customization.</div>\n   453→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   454→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   455→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   456→                        2026-05-13\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Claude Code vs Cursor: two philosophies - Claude Code is terminal-native execution, Cursor is AI-augmented IDE\"</div>\n   459→                </div>\n   460→\n   461→                <div class=\"item\">\n   462→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://geminicli.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI v0.42.0</a></div>\n   463→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Enhanced Memory & Real-Time Voice. Introduces Auto Memory Inbox to automatically capture context from executed commands and files, improved voice input with recording visualizer and output streaming, history command with timeline view and session filtering.</div>\n   464→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   465→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   466→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   467→                        2026-05-12\n   468→                    </div>\n   469→                </div>\n   470→\n   471→                <div class=\"item\">\n   472→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Continue v1.3.38</a></div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Config Management and Security Fixes. Features include .continue/configs support, session history filtering by workspace directory, and critical security vulnerability resolutions. Recent versions added ClawRouter provider for cost-optimized model routing and OpenRouter improvements.</div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   475→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   476→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   477→                        2026-05-10\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                </div>\n   480→\n   481→                <div class=\"item\">\n   482→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.anthropic.com/codex-cli/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI</a></div>\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Chrome Extension & Remote Control. May 2026 updates including Chrome extension for browser automation, remote control capabilities for connecting to remote sessions, CLI 0.130.0 with enhanced stability and new integrations.</div>\n   484→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   485→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   486→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   487→                        2026-05-09\n   488→                    </div>\n   489→                </div>\n   490→\n   491→                <div class=\"item\">\n   492→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a></div>\n   493→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Week 19 Updates: Plugin Support & Enhanced Git Workflows. v2.1.128–v2.1.136 introduces plugin loading from .zip archives and URLs, worktree baseRef configuration, auto mode hard deny rules, and hooks that see active effort level.</div>\n   494→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   495→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   496→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   497→                        2026-05-08\n   498→                    </div>\n   499→                </div>\n   500→\n   501→                <div class=\"item\">\n   502→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-05-06-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-code-april-releases/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot</a></div>\n   503→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Agentic Workflows in VS Code. April 2026 updates focusing on agentic workflows with cloud agent sessions, custom agent capabilities, and Visual Studio April updates. GPT-4.1 deprecated with GPT-5.5 as recommended alternative.</div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   505→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   506→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   507→                        2026-05-06\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                </div>\n   510→\n   511→                <div class=\"item\">\n   512→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://geminicli.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI v0.41.0</a></div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Code Index & Compact Output. Added automatic code indexing on startup with configurable depth control, context menu improvements with global shortcuts and favorite prompts, compact output mode for improved readability.</div>\n   514→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   515→                        <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n   516→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   517→                        2026-05-05\n   518→                    </div>\n   519→                </div>\n   520→\n   521→                <div class=\"item\">\n   522→                    <div class=\"update-title\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.ai/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a></div>\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI-Agentic IDE with Cascade Integration. AI-agentic IDE featuring Cascade for deep codebase context awareness, collaborative editing with real-time AI agent participation, predictive editing for multi-step refactoring.</div>\n   524→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   525→                        <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n   526→                        <span class=\"badge badge-update\">UPDATE</span>\n   527→                        2026-05-01\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                </div>\n   530→            </section>\n   531→\n   532→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   533→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   534→                <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">(20)</span></h2>\n   535→\n   536→                <div class=\"item\">\n   537→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40823421\" target=\"_blank\">The US is winning the AI race in commercialization</a></div>\n   538→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Hacker News community</span> | 2026-05-14</div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Analysis arguing that the US is winning the AI race where it matters most: commercialization and practical application of AI technologies.</div>\n   540→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   541→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   542→                        <span class=\"tag\">commercialization</span>\n   543→                    </div>\n   544→                </div>\n   545→\n   546→                <div class=\"item\">\n   547→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/notion-ai-agent-platform/\" target=\"_blank\">Notion turns workspace into AI agent hub</a></div>\n   548→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Sarah Perez - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-13</div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Notion launched a developer platform that transforms its workspace into a hub for AI agents.</div>\n   550→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   551→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-agents</span>\n   552→                        <span class=\"tag\">notion</span>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                </div>\n   555→\n   556→                <div class=\"item\">\n   557→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/vapi-voice-ai-valuation/\" target=\"_blank\">AI voice startup Vapi hits $500M valuation</a></div>\n   558→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Jagmeet Singh - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-13</div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI voice startup Vapi reached a $500M valuation after winning Amazon Ring as a customer over 40 competitors.</div>\n   560→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   561→                        <span class=\"tag\">voice-ai</span>\n   562→                        <span class=\"tag\">startups</span>\n   563→                    </div>\n   564→                </div>\n   565→\n   566→                <div class=\"item\">\n   567→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/adaption-autoscientist-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">Adaption aims big with AutoScientist</a></div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Russell Brandom - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-13</div>\n   569→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Adaption announced AutoScientist, an AI tool designed to help models train themselves.</div>\n   570→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   571→                        <span class=\"tag\">auto-ml</span>\n   572→                        <span class=\"tag\">self-improving-ai</span>\n   573→                    </div>\n   574→                </div>\n   575→\n   576→                <div class=\"item\">\n   577→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/anthropic-cat-wu-interview/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Cat Wu on AI anticipating user needs</a></div>\n   578→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Lucas Ropek - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-13</div>\n   579→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Anthropic's Cat Wu discussed the future of AI systems that can anticipate user needs before users themselves know what they are.</div>\n   580→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   581→                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   582→                        <span class=\"tag\">proactive-ai</span>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                </div>\n   585→\n   586→                <div class=\"item\">\n   587→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812345\" target=\"_blank\">Leaving GitHub for Forgejo</a></div>\n   588→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">jorijn - Hacker News</span> | 2026-05-13</div>\n   589→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Developer discusses reasons for leaving GitHub for Forgejo, a self-hosted Git forge.</div>\n   590→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   591→                        <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n   592→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   593→                    </div>\n   594→                </div>\n   595→\n   596→                <div class=\"item\">\n   597→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/gm-layoffs-it-ai-skills/\" target=\"_blank\">GM lays off IT workers to hire AI specialists</a></div>\n   598→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Kirsten Korosec - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-12</div>\n   599→                    <div class=\"item-description\">General Motors laid off hundreds of IT workers to hire employees with stronger AI skills.</div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   601→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   602→                        <span class=\"tag\">workforce</span>\n   603→                    </div>\n   604→                </div>\n   605→\n   606→                <div class=\"item\">\n   607→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/google-android-agentic-ai-widgets/\" target=\"_blank\">Google brings agentic AI to Android</a></div>\n   608→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Ivan Mehta - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-12</div>\n   609→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google announced agentic AI capabilities and 'vibe-coded' widgets for Android.</div>\n   610→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   611→                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n   612→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-ai</span>\n   613→                    </div>\n   614→                </div>\n   615→\n   616→                <div class=\"item\">\n   617→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/digg-ai-news-aggregator/\" target=\"_blank\">Digg relaunches as AI news aggregator</a></div>\n   618→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Sarah Perez - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-12</div>\n   619→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Social news pioneer Digg relaunched as an AI-powered news aggregator.</div>\n   620→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   621→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   622→                        <span class=\"tag\">news-aggregation</span>\n   623→                    </div>\n   624→                </div>\n   625→\n   626→                <div class=\"item\">\n   627→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/608\" target=\"_blank\">Amelia Wattenberger on agent-first design</a></div>\n   628→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">The Changelog - Podcast</span> | 2026-05-12</div>\n   629→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Interview about Intent at Augment Code. Key insight: prototyping got easier but finishing got harder.</div>\n   630→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   631→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-ai</span>\n   632→                        <span class=\"tag\">design</span>\n   633→                    </div>\n   634→                </div>\n   635→\n   636→                <div class=\"item\">\n   637→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/11/google-android-show-announcements/\" target=\"_blank\">Googlebooks and vibe-coded widgets</a></div>\n   638→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Sarah Perez, Ivan Mehta - Tech Media</span> | 2026-05-11</div>\n   639→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google announced Googlebooks and vibe-coded widgets at their Android Show event.</div>\n   640→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   641→                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n   642→                        <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   643→                    </div>\n   644→                </div>\n   645→\n   646→                <div class=\"item\">\n   647→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/607\" target=\"_blank\">Astral joins OpenAI</a></div>\n   648→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">The Changelog - Podcast</span> | 2026-05-10</div>\n   649→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Discussion about Astral joining OpenAI and what this signals about developer tools.</div>\n   650→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   651→                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   652→                        <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n   653→                    </div>\n   654→                </div>\n   655→\n   656→                <div class=\"item\">\n   657→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40789234\" target=\"_blank\">A History of IDEs at Google</a></div>\n   658→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">laurentlb - Hacker News</span> | 2026-05-10</div>\n   659→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Detailed discussion about the evolution of IDEs used internally at Google.</div>\n   660→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   661→                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n   662→                        <span class=\"tag\">ides</span>\n   663→                    </div>\n   664→                </div>\n   665→\n   666→                <div class=\"item\">\n   667→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/606\" target=\"_blank\">Tailscale's TSIDP, TSNet, and Aperture</a></div>\n   668→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">The Changelog - Podcast</span> | 2026-05-09</div>\n   669→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Interview about Tailscale's private AI gateway for API key management and agent security.</div>\n   670→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   671→                        <span class=\"tag\">tailscale</span>\n   672→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-gateway</span>\n   673→                    </div>\n   674→                </div>\n   675→\n   676→                <div class=\"item\">\n   677→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/9/webrtc/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI's WebRTC Problem with voice AI</a></div>\n   678→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Luke Curley - Blog</span> | 2026-05-09</div>\n   679→                    <div class=\"item-description\">WebRTC drops audio packets during poor network conditions. For LLM voice prompts, users would rather wait 200ms for accurate prompts than have garbage input.</div>\n   680→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   681→                        <span class=\"tag\">webrtc</span>\n   682→                        <span class=\"tag\">voice-ai</span>\n   683→                    </div>\n   684→                </div>\n   685→\n   686→                <div class=\"item\">\n   687→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/605\" target=\"_blank\">Iran bombed AWS, OpenAI GPT-5.4, brain cells play DOOM</a></div>\n   688→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">The Changelog - Podcast</span> | 2026-05-08</div>\n   689→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Discussion of major AI news including GPT-5.4 with significant coding improvements.</div>\n   690→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   691→                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   692→                        <span class=\"tag\">gpt-5.4</span>\n   693→                    </div>\n   694→                </div>\n   695→\n   696→                <div class=\"item\">\n   697→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/604\" target=\"_blank\">Burke Holland on Opus 4.5 and AI coding</a></div>\n   698→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">The Changelog - Podcast</span> | 2026-05-08</div>\n   699→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Discussion about how Opus 4.5 changed everything in AI coding and GPT-5.3 Codex living up to the hype.</div>\n   700→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   701→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   702→                        <span class=\"tag\">coding</span>\n   703→                    </div>\n   704→                </div>\n   705→\n   706→                <div class=\"item\">\n   707→                    <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/8/html/\" target=\"_blank\">The Unreasonable Effectiveness of HTML</a></div>\n   708→                    <div class=\"insight-meta\"><span class=\"insight-source\">Simon Willison - Blog</span> | 2026-05-08</div>\n   709→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Thariq Shihipar advocates for HTML over Markdown as LLM output format. HTML enables SVG diagrams, interactive widgets, and richer explanations.</div>\n   710→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   711→                        <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n   712→                        <span class=\"tag\">html</span>\n   713→                    </div>\n   714→                </div>\n   715→            </section>\n   716→        </div>\n   717→    </main>\n   718→\n   719→    <footer>\n   720→        <div class=\"container\">\n   721→            <a href=\"#\">Previous Reports</a>\n   722→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   723→            <a href=\"#\">Methodology</a>\n   724→            <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n   725→            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">Report generated by Agent Code Daily - Powered by Claude Agent SDK</p>\n   726→        </div>\n   727→    </footer>\n   728→</body>\n   729→</html>"
